    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Scooter Rental</span>
    <h1>Scooter vs Semi Automatic in Hanoi</h1>
    <p>Every renter in Hanoi meets the same first fork in the road: scooter or semi-automatic. One is twist-and-go, the other has gears for your foot, and both are everywhere in the city's traffic. This guide compares the two types honestly, the mechanism, the experience, the beginner question, and the verified prices of the models in each camp, so you can choose before you arrive instead of dithering at the counter.</p>
    <p>Both camps are represented in our fleet: automatic scooters like the Honda Click, Yamaha Mio, Honda Vision and Honda Air Blade, and semi-automatic underbones like the Honda Wave and Yamaha Sirius. The full verified price list for every model lives on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">rental cost hub</a>, and the scooters have their own <a href="/hanoi-scooter-rental/">Hanoi scooter rental</a> hub.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">The mechanism, in plain words</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">What each feels like in Hanoi traffic</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-3">The beginner question</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-4">The 50cc option, briefly</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-5">Prices: the two camps compared</a></li>
